 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Device and uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A single N-channel enhancement power MOSFET of Infineon's OptiMOS 5 family, rated 100 V, in the 5 mm × 6 mm leadless PG-TDSON-8 (SuperSO8) package. The intended uses are high-performance switch-mode supplies, synchronous rectification among them. Qualification follows JEDEC (J-STD20 and JESD22) for the target applications; leads are lead-free plated, RoHS compliant, and the part is halogen-free to IEC 61249-2-21."
  },
  {
   "topic": "On-resistance and gate drive",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "RDS(on) is 6.0 mΩ typical, 7.0 mΩ max at VGS = 10 V and 40 A; with only 6 V of drive it rises to 7.6 mΩ typical, 10.2 mΩ max at 20 A. Threshold is 2.2 to 3.8 V at 50 µA. Diagram 6 shows the on-resistance climbing steeply at high current with 5 to 6 V of drive, while at 10 V it stays near 6 to 7 mΩ up to 320 A. Diagram 9 has RDS(on) at 10 V and 40 A roughly doubling from 25 °C to 150 °C (about 6 to 11.4 mΩ typical, 13.1 mΩ max)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate charge",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "On the VGS against gate charge curve: Qg(th) is the charge from zero to the threshold voltage; Qgs is the charge from zero to the start of the Miller plateau; Qgd is the charge across the plateau; Qsw runs from the threshold to the end of the plateau, so it is Qgs - Qg(th) + Qgd; Qg is the whole charge to the final gate voltage. At 50 V and 40 A with a 10 V drive these are 6, 10, 6, 11 and 30 nC typical, and the plateau sits at 4.8 V. With the drain held at 0.1 V, Qg(sync) is 26 nC."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal limits",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Junction-to-case resistance through the bottom (the drain pad) is 0.9 K/W typical, 1.5 K/W max; through the top of the package it is 20 K/W max. On the reference board with 6 cm² of drain copper the junction-to-ambient figure is 50 K/W, which limits dissipation to 2.5 W and the continuous drain current to 14 A at TA = 25 °C. With the case held at 25 °C the limits are 83 W and 80 A; Diagram 1 derates power linearly from 25 °C to zero at 150 °C case, and Diagram 2 gives 51 A at 100 °C case."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Avalanche",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Every unit is avalanche tested. The single-pulse rating is 73 mJ at 50 A with RGS = 25 Ω. Diagram 13 gives the permitted avalanche current against avalanche time for starting junction temperatures of 25, 100 and 125 °C, falling from 50 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "The body diode carries 76 A continuous and 320 A pulsed at TC = 25 °C. Forward drop is 0.9 V typical, 1.1 V max at 40 A and 25 °C. Reverse recovery at 50 V, 40 A and 100 A/µs is 53 ns and 89 nC typical (106 ns and 179 nC max)."
  }
 ],
